<title>USA: Mylan gets FDA approval to market capsules.</title>
<headline>Mylan gets FDA approval to market capsules.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH, Pa. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mylan Laboratories Inc said on Thursday that it has received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to manufacture and market Nitrofurantoin capsules in 50 mg and 100 mg strengths.</p>
<p>Nitrofurantoin is the generic version of Procter &amp; Gamble Co's Macrodantin, an antibacterial agent used to treat urinary tract infections.</p>
